  "description": "Relay: a hub pre-splits a long line into two parts (one action each, presplit, part n/of), results carry t{wait_ms, send_ms}, the platform echoes come back as self lines with relay_ref so the hub marks them echoed instead of ingesting them. Then an oversized presplit part is refused (relay_refused, too_long), a relay into a switched-off binding fails (binding_off), and a bot-authored reply keeps 1.0 behaviour.",
